## 🧪 INTEGRATION TEST ARCHITECTURE RULES

### **TEST RULE #1: REAL USER CREATION PATTERN**

**NEVER create users directly in database for integration tests**

❌ **WRONG PATTERN**:
```javascript
// ❌ WRONG: Direct database user creation
await supabase.from('users').insert({ email, password_hash });
```

✅ **REQUIRED PATTERN**:
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Real authentication flow
async function createRealTestUser(userSuffix = '') {
  const signupResponse = await supertest(app)
    .post('/v1/auth/signup')
    .send({
      name: `Test User ${userSuffix}`,
      email: `test-${Date.now()}-${userSuffix}@example.com`,
      password: 'TestPassword123!'
    });
    
  return { 
    id: signupResponse.body.userId, 
    jwtToken: signupResponse.body.jwtToken 
  };
}
```

### **TEST RULE #2: ERROR CLASSIFICATION FRAMEWORK**

**NEVER treat configuration bugs as legitimate integration behavior**

✅ **REQUIRED ERROR CLASSIFICATION**:
```javascript
const classifyWorkoutLogError = (error) => {
  const errorMessage = error.message || '';
  
  const classification = {
    // Configuration bugs (MUST FAIL TESTS)
    isConfigurationBug: errorMessage.includes('relation') && errorMessage.includes('does not exist') ||
                       errorMessage.includes('column') && errorMessage.includes('does not exist') ||
                       errorMessage.includes('function') && errorMessage.includes('does not exist'),
    
    // Legitimate integration errors (SHOULD PASS TESTS)  
    isConnectionError: errorMessage.includes('ENOTFOUND') || errorMessage.includes('network'),
    isValidationError: errorMessage.includes('validation') || errorMessage.includes('constraint'),
    isAuthError: errorMessage.includes('unauthorized') || errorMessage.includes('invalid token'),
    
    shouldFailTest: false,
    shouldPassTest: true
  };
  
  if (classification.isConfigurationBug) {
    classification.shouldFailTest = true;
    classification.shouldPassTest = false;
    throw error; // Configuration bugs MUST fail tests
  }
  
  return classification;
};
```

